title: Entity classes document only a subset of their fields
updated: 2026-08-28T00:26:18Z
---

Found during the pre-release audit and confirmed while closing #68.

The four older entity classes carry `has` declarations with no `=attr` block
at all, so the woven POD documents a subset of what the object actually
answers to:

  API::Docker::Volume   CreatedAt, Status, Labels, Scope, Options, UsageData
  API::Docker::Container, ::Image, ::Network  -- same pattern, a
    representative subset documented rather than every daemon field

The three entity classes added in this round (Plugin, Secret, Config) document
every field they carry, so the convention the distribution follows now is the
complete one -- these four predate it.

Not release-blocking: nothing is wrong, only absent, and the accessors work
whether or not they are documented. It is inconsistency rather than error.

Two things to decide before doing it:
  - whether every daemon field deserves an =attr, or whether a class should
    document the ones a caller has reason to touch and say so. The daemon
    response for a container is enormous; documenting all of it would bury
    the useful half.
  - where the descriptions come from. For #68 the RFC3339 shape of
    CreatedAt/UpdatedAt was taken from a captured fixture rather than
    guessed, and that is the standard to hold: a description that invents a
    format is worse than no description.

Related: #68, which closed the same gap for Secret and Config.
